# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/TOSO_c6ad489d_cdcc_4a0e_b1c6_6ea89ffebefb> (sexual reproduction)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/TOSO_c6ad489d_cdcc_4a0e_b1c6_6ea89ffebefb> "Depending on context sex can have distinct definitions 

Different terms that could describe or have been used to describe what sex represents (Autho: Caitlin McDonough-Goldstein).

Should the ToS Ontology start describing individuals with a preferred term different thanjust \"sex\"?


Reproductive category
Sex category
Reproductive expression
Sex expression
Reproductive phenotype
Sexual phenotype
Reproductive modality
Sexual modality
Reproductive morph
Sexual morph
Reproductive role
Sexual role
Reproductive allocation strategy
Sex allocation strategy
Reproductive type
Sexual type")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/TOSO_c6ad489d_cdcc_4a0e_b1c6_6ea89ffebefb> "sexual reproduction"@en)
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/TOSO_c6ad489d_cdcc_4a0e_b1c6_6ea89ffebefb> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/TOSO_80229d74_f397_4f1e_98a0_9fd3d9addca7>)


